    meaning: "Arjuna acknowledges Krishna's supremacy even over Brahma the creator. He lists profound names: Ananta (infinite), Devesa (Lord of gods), Jagannivasa (abode of the universe), and identifies Krishna as the imperishable (akshara), both the manifest and unmanifest, and the supreme reality beyond both.",
